# Publish

<h2 id="wg-094">Check facts, language and presentation separately</h2>

One person checking all three at once misses things. Check that it is true, then that it is clear, then that it looks right and works with a screen reader.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Looks fine. | Facts: checked against the integration docs. Language: read aloud, no jargon. Presentation: checked at 320px wide and with a screen reader. |

<h2 id="wg-095">Report checks within their limits</h2>

Say what you checked and what you did not. A passing test is not proof that people understand it.

<%= example('wg-review-record') %>

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Fully accessible and tested. | Checked with an automated tool and with the keyboard only. Not yet tested with a screen reader. |
| Passed review. | Reviewed 11 November 2026. No live appliance was operated. |

<h2 id="wg-086">Describe accessibility evidence accurately</h2>

Do not claim a page is accessible. Say what was tested.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| This page meets WCAG. | We tested this page with a keyboard and an automated checker. We found no problems. We have not tested it with a screen reader. |

## Ask someone who did not write it to try it

Ask a person who did not write the steps to follow them with the device in front of them. Record what happened, including where they stopped.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Steps checked by the author. | Followed by one household member with the light in front of them. They stopped at step 3 because the button label differed. We changed the label and they finished. |

## Before you publish

- the content has an owner and a source
- it uses the words from [A to Z Technical](../style-guides/technical-a-to-z.html)
- any state or confirmation matches what the integration can really report
- each question and link follows the [writing guidelines](../writing-guidelines/index.html)
